# gVRMod — OpenXR module + dual-backend Lua addon

Native **OpenXR** binary (`gmcl_vrmod_xr_*`) and one client Lua addon tree.

## Why only one Lua addon?

There used to be two copies (`addon/gvrmod` + `vrmod-x64`). That was accidental dual-SoT thrash.

**Now there is one:**

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| **`addon/vrmod-x64/`** | **Only** client addon (git submodule → [vrmod-x64](https://github.com/Abyss-c0re/vrmod-x64)) |
| `src/` + CMake | OpenXR native module |
| `install.sh` | Installs XR binary + this addon |

The same Lua tree works with **OpenVR** (`gmcl_vrmod_*`) or **OpenXR** (`gmcl_vrmod_xr_*`) via auto-detect (`vrmod_backend` / `vrmod_prefer_backend`).

Edit Lua **only** under `addon/vrmod-x64/`. Then:

```bash
./scripts/sync_vrmod_x64.sh    # commit submodule + bump parent pointer
# or rely on ./scripts/install_git_hooks.sh pre-commit
```

## Dual native modules (no filename clash)

| Backend | Binary | `require` |
|---------|--------|-----------|
| **OpenVR** | `gmcl_vrmod_linux64.dll` / `gmcl_vrmod_win64.dll` | `"vrmod"` |
| **OpenXR** (this repo) | `gmcl_vrmod_xr_linux64.dll` / `gmcl_vrmod_xr_win64.dll` | `"vrmod_xr"` |

Both may sit in `garrysmod/lua/bin` at once. Lua loads one (`vrmod_prefer_backend` = `auto` \| `openxr` \| `openvr`).

```
vrmod_backend
```

## Clone

```bash
git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/Abyss-c0re/gVRMod.git
# or:
git submodule update --init --recursive
./scripts/install_git_hooks.sh
```

## Build / install

**Linux**
```bash
./build.sh
./install.sh
# → gmcl_vrmod_xr_linux64.dll + garrysmod/addons/vrmod-x64/
```

**Windows**
```bat
build.bat
# → install\GarrysMod\garrysmod\lua\bin\gmcl_vrmod_xr_win64.dll
```

| Platform | Graphics | Texture share | RT flip |
|----------|----------|---------------|---------|
| **Linux x64** | OpenGL (GLX / togl) | glGenTextures + FBO observation | **1** |
| **Windows x64** | D3D11 | D3D9 CreateTexture hook (module-master main) | **0** |

## Module version

**v27** — `GetBackend()` · dual binary names · full restart teardown.

